attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 2, `cutA` to `dicD`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 1% of calls {S1}. The model names 95 to 99% of them, fewest at column 1, `dsbD`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `cadC`**, column 3, carried by 84%, with a second family in 19% {S2.c3}. Then columns 4 to 8, `cadB` to `ghoT`, are [[lysine decarboxylation and transport]], carried by 85 to 86% {S2.c4-8, Q}. Through columns 47 to 49 a branch of 3 shell families runs in 12 to 14%, and through columns 53 to 58 a branch of 6 shell families runs in 12 to 19% {S2.b47, S2.b53}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 85%, and hesitates less there, 0.06 against 0.73 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 3, `cadC`, a fork column, 2.48 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 76 to 79, `pdeC` to `uvrA`, are carried by 44 to 59% of chromosomes {S2.c76, S2.c79}. The last column is `uvrA`, in 44% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 86% of genes**, 0.70 bits on average, perplexity 2.1 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.80 against 0.21 bits, and names fewer genes, 67% against 94% {C}.

